  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life-saving emergency livelihood response in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce the adverse impact of flooding on the lives and livelihoods of 65,000 vulnerable households in South Sudan, particularly those at
heightened risk due to escalating conflict, anticipated floods, food insecurity, and the ongoing cholera outbreak. The intervention will focus
on the most affected counties, namely Canal/Pigi, Fangak, Akobo, Ayod, Panyikang, and Fashoda.</narrative>
  </description>
